      "writtenOn": "2026-11-26T09:18:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Each test class calls `random.seed(config.rnd_seed)`. Keeping that seed lets us replay the packet inputs. It also gives concurrent classes the same sequence. In the six-job pilot with a fixed seed, a namespace fixture exhausted all five attempts because the generated names collided.\n\nA private PRNG seeded independently in each worker would also work. I used `SystemRandom` for the namespace and veth suffixes so they get independent names even when workers replay the same seed or inherit state through `fork`. That keeps the logic local to the resources that have to be unique in the shared kernel.",
      "parentUuid": "da6bb2f3_11f96731",
